A||N||6||gargoyle||Carbon Fiber for custom Aus center console||||5||
Z||000000||gargoyle||09-05-2001||11:35 AM||||With any luck my new console  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> from the mighty Aus should arrive today. My question is this. I am using this as a place for some stereo bit so Aus made it with a door for me. He said the tolerance is pretty tight. I was thinking that instead of using upholstery on it I would cover just the door with carbon fiber. I not sure if I'm going to use the fake stuff or the real thing. Just looking for opinions or ideas. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||artherd||09-05-2001||03:10 PM||||I do a fair bit of work with carbonfibre, it's great stuff!!<P>Works much like fiberglass, only you need to step the quality waaaay up...<P>When cured, it is precision-machineable, so extreemely tight clearances are no problem. It has better expansion/contraction chareristics than any other material in the Fiero too :P)<P>It is expensive though, but worth it.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gargoyle:<BR><B>With any luck my new console   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> from the mighty Aus should arrive today. My question is this. I am using this as a place for some stereo bit so Aus made it with a door for me. He said the tolerance is pretty tight. I was thinking that instead of using upholstery on it I would cover just the door with carbon fiber. I not sure if I'm going to use the fake stuff or the real thing. Just looking for opinions or ideas. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000002||TI_3VOM||09-05-2001||11:00 PM||||Since someone brought up carbon fiber, I thought I'd ask: has anyone tried to replicate body panels for the Fiero? Whether it's an original body style or just repoductions, how expensive would that be to produce? Or how about an underbody tray, ala the Ferrari 355? (the questions I come up with)||||reg||5
Z||000003||Sootah||09-05-2001||11:58 PM||||What are the benefits of Carbon fiber over fiberglass? Which is easier to work with? Which costs more, and by how much? Soon enough I will need to start doing custom stuff to my soon-to-be Fiero. This info would be helpful.<P>Thanx||||reg||1
Z||000004||artherd||09-06-2001||12:09 AM||||First things first, carbonfibre costs between 100 and 1000 times more than glassfibre (depending on how it is formed)<BR>...    <BR>...   <BR>let that sink in  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>That said, it is otherwise an all around supior material.   (just about as easy to work as glassfibre, but you need to step the cleanliness and precision up an order of magnitude)<P>Carbonfibre is far far stronger, and lighter, and can take higher tempratures (mostly a function of the expxies used.) and has incredible shape-memory.  you can tie a sheet up, and leave it for a week, come back, and undo it.  it will *snap* back perfectly flat.<P>Did I mention it's insanely strong and light?<P>Now, glassfibre is generally easier to finish smooth and paint (more steps with carbon, and you need special primers.)<P><BR>I am working on some Fiero carbon parts,<BR>first will come the doorskins  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (going to take a while for me, the carbon cloth alone is going to cost several $hundred/side, and I've got lotsa other projects demanding my money lately  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Eventually I hope to have carbon replacements for all the plastic body components (that sag over time, this includes front/rear fenders, doorskins, and the front and rear fascias, the hardest part.) and maybe a hood and decklid too.  Those will be really pricy though. sigh.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Sootah:<BR><B>What are the benefits of Carbon fiber over fiberglass? Which is easier to work with? Which costs more, and by how much? Soon enough I will need to start doing custom stuff to my soon-to-be Fiero. This info would be helpful.<P>Thanx</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000005||Sootah||09-06-2001||12:58 AM||||How hard would a spoiler be to build? And how well will fiberglass bind to the body panels (if at all)?||||reg||1
Z||000006||AusFiero||09-06-2001||03:02 AM||||I wish I had known you like carbon fibre gargoyle. I have stick on stuff that looks very convincing as used on my interior. <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
